    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d691">

                <pb facs="0583" n="467" xml:id="pg467"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        certain American diplomatic missions.</hi><anchor
                        n="11" xml:id="d691-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-17T21:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 17, 1914, 9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s April 15th, 8 p.m. General Huerta yesterday signified his
                    willingness to have the required salute given if this Government would salute
                    the Mexican flag simultaneously.</p>
                <p>For information of the Government to which you are accredited Department’s reply
                    is given:</p>
                <p>[Quotation of telegram 754 of April 17, 12 m., to Chargé O’Shaughnessy.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d691-f1" n="11" type="source" xml:id="d691-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the Embassies at Paris, London, Madrid, Rome, Berlin and Vienna.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
